#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:32
msgid ""
"This Easter egg answers the perennial request to replace indentation with "
"curly braces. Attempting it raises ``SyntaxError: not a chance``."
msgstr ""
"Este huevo de pascua responde a la eterna petición de sustituir la sangría "
"por llaves. Intentarlo lanza ``SyntaxError: not a chance``."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:36
msgid "How is the Zen of Python text stored inside the ``this`` module?"
msgstr ""
"¿Cómo se almacena el texto del Zen de Python dentro del módulo ``this``?"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:45
msgid "As plain text."
msgstr "Como texto plano."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:46
msgid "Base64 encoded."
msgstr "Codificado en Base64."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:47
msgid "ROT13 encoded."
msgstr "Codificado en ROT13."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:48
msgid "Compressed with gzip."
msgstr "Comprimido con gzip."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:53
msgid ""
"Fittingly obfuscated, the Zen text in ``this.py`` is stored ROT13 encoded "
"and decoded at import time using a small character-translation dictionary."
msgstr ""
"Convenientemente ofuscado, el texto del Zen en ``this.py`` se almacena "
"codificado en ROT13 y se decodifica al importarlo mediante un pequeño "
"diccionario de traducción de caracteres."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:57
msgid ""
"Which earlier language, which Guido helped develop at CWI, strongly "
"influenced Python?"
msgstr ""
"¿Qué lenguaje anterior, en cuyo desarrollo colaboró Guido en el CWI, influyó"
" fuertemente en Python?"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:66
msgid "Pascal."
msgstr "Pascal."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:67
msgid "Modula-3."
msgstr "Modula-3."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:68
msgid "ABC."
msgstr "ABC."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:69
msgid "Smalltalk."
msgstr "Smalltalk."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:74
msgid ""
"Python was heavily influenced by ABC, a teaching language Guido had worked "
"on at CWI. He kept ABC's readability while fixing what he saw as its "
"shortcomings."
msgstr ""
"Python estuvo muy influido por ABC, un lenguaje didáctico en el que Guido "
"había trabajado en el CWI. Conservó la legibilidad de ABC mientras corregía "
"lo que consideraba sus carencias."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:79
msgid "In which country did Guido van Rossum begin developing Python at CWI?"
msgstr "¿En qué país empezó Guido van Rossum a desarrollar Python en el CWI?"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:88
msgid "The United States."
msgstr "Estados Unidos."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:89
msgid "Germany."
msgstr "Alemania."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:90
msgid "Belgium."
msgstr "Bélgica."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:91
msgid "The Netherlands."
msgstr "Los Países Bajos."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:96
msgid ""
"Guido started Python at CWI, the national research institute for mathematics"
" and computer science in the Netherlands. The Zen even winks at this with "
"\"unless you're Dutch\"."
msgstr ""
"Guido empezó Python en el CWI, el instituto nacional de investigación en "
"matemáticas e informática de los Países Bajos. El Zen incluso hace un guiño "
"a esto con \"a menos que seas neerlandés\"."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:101
msgid "What is the final aphorism of the Zen of Python?"
msgstr "¿Cuál es el último aforismo del Zen de Python?"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:110 ../../../culture-hard.rst:390
msgid "\"Readability counts.\""
msgstr "\"La legibilidad cuenta.\""

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:111
msgid "\"Namespaces are one honking great idea -- let's do more of those!\""
msgstr "\"¡Los espacios de nombres son una idea genial, hagamos más de esos!\""

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:112 ../../../culture-hard.rst:392
msgid "\"Now is better than never.\""
msgstr "\"Ahora es mejor que nunca.\""

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:113
msgid "\"Simple is better than complex.\""
msgstr "\"Simple es mejor que complejo.\""

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:118
msgid ""
"The Zen closes on an upbeat note: \"Namespaces are one honking great idea --"
" let's do more of those!\""
msgstr ""
"El Zen se cierra con una nota optimista: \"¡Los espacios de nombres son una "
"idea genial, hagamos más de esos!\""

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:122
msgid "Which special (\"dunder\") method implements the ``<`` operator?"
msgstr "¿Qué método especial (\"dunder\") implementa el operador ``<``?"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:131
msgid "``__less__``"
msgstr "``__less__``"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:132
msgid "``__lt__``"
msgstr "``__lt__``"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:133
msgid "``__cmp__``"
msgstr "``__cmp__``"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:134
msgid "``__min__``"
msgstr "``__min__``"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:139
msgid ""
"Python calls ``__lt__`` (short for \"less than\") to evaluate the ``<`` "
"operator between two objects."
msgstr ""
"Python llama a ``__lt__`` (abreviatura de \"less than\", menor que) para "
"evaluar el operador ``<`` entre dos objetos."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:143
msgid "Which statement about CPython's GIL is true?"
msgstr "¿Cuál de estas afirmaciones sobre el GIL de CPython es cierta?"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:152
msgid "It lets any number of threads run Python bytecode simultaneously."
msgstr ""
"Permite que cualquier número de hilos ejecute bytecode de Python de forma "
"simultánea."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:153
msgid "It is a feature of every Python implementation, including Jython."
msgstr ""
"Es una característica de todas las implementaciones de Python, incluida "
"Jython."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:154
msgid "It allows only one thread to execute Python bytecode at a time."
msgstr "Solo permite que un hilo ejecute bytecode de Python a la vez."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:155
msgid "It only affects programs that use ``asyncio``."
msgstr "Solo afecta a los programas que usan ``asyncio``."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:160
msgid ""
"The Global Interpreter Lock permits just one thread to run Python bytecode "
"at a time in CPython. Implementations like Jython have no GIL."
msgstr ""
"El Global Interpreter Lock permite que en CPython solo un hilo ejecute "
"bytecode de Python a la vez. Implementaciones como Jython no tienen GIL."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:164
msgid "Which Python release first introduced f-strings?"
msgstr "¿Qué versión de Python introdujo por primera vez las f-strings?"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:173 ../../../culture-hard.rst:214
msgid "Python 3.4."
msgstr "Python 3.4."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:174 ../../../culture-hard.rst:194
#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:215
msgid "Python 3.5."
msgstr "Python 3.5."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:175 ../../../culture-hard.rst:195
#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:216
msgid "Python 3.6."
msgstr "Python 3.6."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:176 ../../../culture-hard.rst:197
msgid "Python 3.8."
msgstr "Python 3.8."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:181
msgid ""
"Formatted string literals (f-strings), specified in PEP 498, arrived in "
"Python 3.6."
msgstr ""
"Los literales de cadena formateados (f-strings), especificados en la PEP "
"498, llegaron en Python 3.6."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:185
msgid "Which Python release introduced the walrus operator (``:=``)?"
msgstr "¿Qué versión de Python introdujo el operador morsa (``:=``)?"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:196 ../../../culture-hard.rst:217
msgid "Python 3.7."
msgstr "Python 3.7."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:202
msgid "The walrus operator from PEP 572 shipped in Python 3.8."
msgstr "El operador morsa de la PEP 572 llegó en Python 3.8."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:205
msgid "In which Python release did PEP 484 type hints first become available?"
msgstr ""
"¿En qué versión de Python pasaron a estar disponibles por primera vez las "
"anotaciones de tipo de la PEP 484?"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:222
msgid ""
"PEP 484 and the ``typing`` module landed in Python 3.5, giving Python a "
"standard syntax for type annotations."
msgstr ""
"La PEP 484 y el módulo ``typing`` llegaron en Python 3.5, dotando a Python "
"de una sintaxis estándar para las anotaciones de tipo."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:226
msgid "What was the standard tool for migrating Python 2 code to Python 3?"
msgstr ""
"¿Cuál era la herramienta estándar para migrar código de Python 2 a Python 3?"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:235
msgid "``pyupgrade``"
msgstr "``pyupgrade``"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:236
msgid "``py23``"
msgstr "``py23``"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:237
msgid "``2to3``"
msgstr "``2to3``"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:238
msgid "``modernize``"
msgstr "``modernize``"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:243
msgid ""
"``2to3`` was the tool shipped with Python that automatically rewrote many "
"Python 2 constructs into their Python 3 equivalents."
msgstr ""
"``2to3`` era la herramienta que venía con Python y que reescribía "
"automáticamente muchas construcciones de Python 2 en sus equivalentes de "
"Python 3."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:247
msgid ""
"Which of these is a real feature you can enable with ``from __future__ "
"import``?"
msgstr ""
"¿Cuál de estas es una funcionalidad real que puedes habilitar con ``from "
"__future__ import``?"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:256
msgid "``goto``"
msgstr "``goto``"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:257
msgid "``switch``"
msgstr "``switch``"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:258
msgid "``annotations``"
msgstr "``annotations``"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:259
msgid "``macros``"
msgstr "``macros``"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:264
msgid ""
"``from __future__ import annotations`` (PEP 563) makes annotations be stored"
" as strings rather than evaluated at definition time. The others are not "
"``__future__`` features."
msgstr ""
"``from __future__ import annotations`` (PEP 563) hace que las anotaciones se"
" almacenen como cadenas en lugar de evaluarse en el momento de la "
"definición. Las demás no son funcionalidades de ``__future__``."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:269
msgid ""
"The debate over which feature is often cited as a factor in Guido stepping "
"down as BDFL?"
msgstr ""
"¿El debate sobre qué funcionalidad se cita a menudo como un factor en la "
"retirada de Guido como BDFL?"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:278
msgid "f-strings."
msgstr "Las f-strings."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:279
msgid "Type hints."
msgstr "Las anotaciones de tipo."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:280
msgid "The walrus operator (PEP 572)."
msgstr "El operador morsa (PEP 572)."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:281
msgid "Async/await."
msgstr "Async/await."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:286
msgid ""
"The contentious debate around PEP 572's walrus operator is widely cited as "
"part of what led Guido to step down as BDFL in 2018."
msgstr ""
"El polémico debate en torno al operador morsa de la PEP 572 se cita "
"ampliamente como parte de lo que llevó a Guido a dejar el cargo de BDFL en "
"2018."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:290
msgid ""
"After Guido stepped down, how is Python's language governance now organized?"
msgstr ""
"Tras la retirada de Guido, ¿cómo se organiza ahora la gobernanza del "
"lenguaje Python?"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:299
msgid "A single successor BDFL was appointed."
msgstr "Se nombró a un único BDFL sucesor."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:300
msgid "An elected Steering Council."
msgstr "Un Steering Council elegido."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:301
msgid "A public shareholder vote."
msgstr "Una votación pública de accionistas."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:302
msgid "The decision was handed to the PyPI maintainers."
msgstr "La decisión se dejó en manos de los mantenedores de PyPI."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:307
msgid ""
"Since 2019 the language has been governed by an elected Steering Council "
"(PEP 13) rather than a single benevolent dictator."
msgstr ""
"Desde 2019 el lenguaje se gobierna mediante un Steering Council elegido (PEP"
" 13) en lugar de un único dictador benévolo."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:311
msgid ""
"The Easter egg ``from __future__ import barry_as_FLUFL`` re-enables which "
"old operator?"
msgstr ""
"El huevo de pascua ``from __future__ import barry_as_FLUFL`` vuelve a "
"habilitar ¿qué antiguo operador?"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:325
msgid "The backtick ``repr`` operator."
msgstr "El operador ``repr`` con comillas invertidas."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:326
msgid "The ``print`` statement."
msgstr "La sentencia ``print``."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:327
msgid "The ``<>`` \"not equal\" operator."
msgstr "El operador ``<>`` de \"distinto de\"."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:328
msgid "Integer division with ``/``."
msgstr "La división entera con ``/``."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:333
msgid ""
"This joke (PEP 401) honors Barry Warsaw as the \"Friendly Language Uncle For"
" Life\" by temporarily bringing back Python 2's ``<>`` not-equal operator, "
"so ``1 <> 2`` evaluates to ``True``."
msgstr ""
"Esta broma (PEP 401) rinde homenaje a Barry Warsaw como \"Friendly Language "
"Uncle For Life\" recuperando temporalmente el operador de desigualdad ``<>``"
" de Python 2, de modo que ``1 <> 2`` se evalúa como ``True``."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:338
msgid ""
"Which pair of names, alongside Guido van Rossum, are listed as authors of "
"PEP 8?"
msgstr ""
"¿Qué par de nombres, junto a Guido van Rossum, figuran como autores de la "
"PEP 8?"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:347
msgid "Tim Peters and Raymond Hettinger."
msgstr "Tim Peters y Raymond Hettinger."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:348
msgid "Barry Warsaw and Nick Coghlan."
msgstr "Barry Warsaw y Nick Coghlan."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:349
msgid "Brett Cannon and Alex Martelli."
msgstr "Brett Cannon y Alex Martelli."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:350
msgid "Kenneth Reitz and David Beazley."
msgstr "Kenneth Reitz y David Beazley."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:355
msgid ""
"PEP 8, the style guide, is credited to Guido van Rossum, Barry Warsaw, and "
"Nick Coghlan."
msgstr ""
"La PEP 8, la guía de estilo, se atribuye a Guido van Rossum, Barry Warsaw y "
"Nick Coghlan."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:359
msgid ""
"In the *Monty Python* \"Spam\" sketch that inspired Python's placeholder "
"names, where is it set?"
msgstr ""
"En el sketch \"Spam\" de *Monty Python* que inspiró los nombres de relleno "
"de Python, ¿dónde transcurre?"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:368
msgid "A pet shop."
msgstr "Una tienda de mascotas."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:369
msgid "A café where nearly every menu item contains spam."
msgstr "Un café donde casi todos los platos de la carta contienen spam."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:370
msgid "A courtroom."
msgstr "Una sala de tribunal."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:371
msgid "A cheese shop."
msgstr "Una quesería."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:376
msgid ""
"The sketch takes place in a café whose menu is overrun with spam, which is "
"why ``spam`` (and ``eggs``) became Python's go-to example names."
msgstr ""
"El sketch transcurre en un café cuya carta está plagada de spam, y por eso "
"``spam`` (y ``eggs``) se convirtieron en los nombres de ejemplo por "
"excelencia de Python."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:380
msgid ""
"Which value does the Zen of Python associate specifically with \"you're "
"Dutch\"?"
msgstr ""
"¿Qué valor asocia el Zen de Python específicamente con \"eres neerlandés\"?"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:389
msgid "\"Errors should never pass silently.\""
msgstr "\"Los errores nunca deberían pasar en silencio.\""

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:391
msgid "\"There should be one obvious way to do it.\""
msgstr "\"Debería haber una forma obvia de hacerlo.\""

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:397
msgid ""
"The Zen follows \"There should be one-- and preferably only one --obvious "
"way to do it.\" with the wink \"Although that way may not be obvious at "
"first unless you're Dutch.\" -- a nod to Guido's nationality."
msgstr ""
"El Zen continúa \"Debería haber una -y preferiblemente solo una- forma obvia"
" de hacerlo.\" con el guiño \"Aunque esa forma quizá no sea obvia a primera "
"vista a menos que seas neerlandés.\", un guiño a la nacionalidad de Guido."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:402
msgid "At which company did Guido van Rossum work from 2005 to 2012?"
msgstr "¿En qué empresa trabajó Guido van Rossum de 2005 a 2012?"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:411
msgid "Microsoft."
msgstr "Microsoft."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:412
msgid "Dropbox."
msgstr "Dropbox."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:413
msgid "Google."
msgstr "Google."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:414
msgid "Red Hat."
msgstr "Red Hat."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:419
msgid ""
"Guido van Rossum worked at Google from 2005 to 2012 (where he spent part of "
"his time on Python), then at Dropbox until 2019, and later joined Microsoft "
"in 2020."
msgstr ""
"Guido van Rossum trabajó en Google de 2005 a 2012 (donde dedicó parte de su "
"tiempo a Python), luego en Dropbox hasta 2019 y más tarde se incorporó a "
"Microsoft en 2020."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:424
msgid ""
"Which experimental CPython build, added in Python 3.13, can run without the "
"GIL?"
msgstr ""
"¿Qué compilación experimental de CPython, añadida en Python 3.13, puede "
"ejecutarse sin el GIL?"

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:433
msgid "The \"stackless\" build."
msgstr "La compilación \"stackless\"."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:434
msgid "The \"free-threaded\" (no-GIL) build."
msgstr "La compilación \"free-threaded\" (sin GIL)."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:435
msgid "The \"async\" build."
msgstr "La compilación \"async\"."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:436
msgid "The \"JIT-only\" build."
msgstr "La compilación \"JIT-only\"."

#: ../../../culture-hard.rst:441
msgid ""
"PEP 703 introduced an experimental *free-threaded* build of CPython in "
"Python 3.13 that can run without the Global Interpreter Lock, allowing true "
"parallelism across threads."
msgstr ""
"La PEP 703 introdujo en Python 3.13 una compilación experimental *free-"
"threaded* de CPython que puede ejecutarse sin el Global Interpreter Lock, "
"permitiendo un paralelismo real entre hilos."

